cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "RNAseqLab: An Interactive Platform for RNA-seq Differential Expression and Functional Interpretation"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Yerushalmy
    given-names: Yonatan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2671-2457"

  - family-names: Amir
    given-names: Rachel

abstract: >-
  RNAseqLab is a local, interactive R Shiny platform for differential
  expression analysis and downstream biological interpretation of RNA-seq
  data. It integrates data import and quality assessment, differential
  expression testing, expression heatmaps, exploratory and publication-ready
  visualization, functional and pathway enrichment, gene annotation,
  specialized organism-specific analyses, and automated report generation
  within a unified workflow. Its gene set enrichment analysis uses ranked
  results across all tested genes and supports GO, KEGG, Hallmark, plant
  metabolic network, Arabidopsis transposable-element superfamily, and custom
  gene sets. RNAseqLab also provides transcript and isoform analysis, including
  differential transcript usage and isoform-switching summaries, with
  transcript-to-gene mappings supplied directly or derived from GTF/GFF files.
  The application accepts differential-expression results, raw count matrices,
  and transcript-quantification outputs generated by RSEM, featureCounts,
  Salmon, or Kallisto. By combining established bioinformatics methods with an
  accessible graphical interface, RNAseqLab enables researchers to perform
  reproducible downstream RNA-seq analyses locally without requiring
  command-line programming.

keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - R Shiny
  - DESeq2
  - gene set enrichment analysis
  - GSEA
  - functional enrichment
  - expression heatmap
  - transcript-level analysis
  - differential transcript usage
  - isoform switching
  - transcript-to-gene mapping
  - RSEM
  - Salmon
  - Kallisto
  - bioinformatics

